// Section info (longer explanation, shown on hover / in the info box)
"settings.info.language"      = "The chosen language filters the TTS voices shown below and sets the default recognition locale. The interface language is changed at the bottom of this page.";
"settings.info.voice"         = "Each voice is a small neural embedding (≈500 KB) downloaded locally. The picker shows only voices installed for the current language; uninstalled ones are greyed out.";
"settings.info.stt"           = "Apple Speech is the system recognizer (low cost, high quality, requires macOS Dictation to be enabled). Whisper is a local ggml model (~465 MB), fully offline. Switching restarts the helper — a few hundred milliseconds.";
"settings.info.commands"      = "Each action has one or more synonyms. Words can be in any language — they aren't translated, the raw audio is what matters. Words already used by another action will be rejected to avoid ambiguity.";
"settings.info.text-prep"     = "A chunk is the atomic unit of synthesis and voice navigation. Smaller chunks = snappier command response and finer jumps, but more fragmentation. Changes require re-importing existing documents. The audio cache holds synthesized FLACs; clearing it loses no work, only regeneration time.";
"settings.info.installations" = "Marginalia runs offline. Only in this section, and only when you explicitly act, may the app reach huggingface.co and github.com to download missing models. All assets are Apache-2.0 or MIT.";
"settings.info.theme"         = "Changes the accent tint — highlights, player pill, audio bars, note hover. The warm-dark background stays — it's part of Marginalia's identity.";
"settings.info.diagnostics"   = "Live provider status and filesystem paths. Includes the last ApplyReport (elapsed time, what was swapped). Handy when something isn't working — selectable for copy-paste.";
"settings.info.interface"     = "Different from the reading/recognition language in the Language section: here you pick the language the app itself speaks to you — menus, buttons, Settings.";

